Performance:
=== Empty ===

--------------------------------------------------

Countdown:
This countdown indicates to the player how long it is till the server starts. During this time the players should be locked into the lobby. When the
countdown reaches zero the a start sequence should be run (something like reset time and wether) and the players should now be allowed to leave the
lobby. The countdown can be startet by an admin and should also be persistant towards server restarts.

Playertime counter:
The plugin should count the playtime of the players and also categorize it by sessions and world (main, different event worlds, lobby, etc). With
this data the server should create a statistical overview which the players can look up if they want. Also the admins should be able to look up 
individual player playtime and there also should be a general overview over overall server statistics like, how many players are online over time.
Also the admin should be able to output a list of the players sortet by things like their overall playtime, longest session or last recorded session.

Editable menus:
Make it so the players are able to edit the layout of their menus themselves. They should be able to change the position of different buttons on the
menu and also hide irrelevant content. They should not be able to move items from one menu into another and also not the general controls (back,
close, forward). These edits shall be made through a gui being enabled by a new button in the menu which is in the bottom right corner of the menu
(inside the outer ring).

Night vision toggle:
There should be a toggle for the players to enable or disable night vision. If night vision is enbaled the player should receive the night vision
effect (without any particles). Every player has his individual toggle. The toggle should be accessable via a menu button or the /nightvision 
command. In the config.yml there should he a field "night-vision-toggle". This field should receive a boolean which determines whether players can
use the toggle or not. If not every player has night vision disabled. Admins should also be able to change the setting with "/admin config
night-vision-toggle true|false". This should also change the state in the config file.

Event inspect:
Admins should be able to go into event world in spectator mode during the building phase. When the admin tipes "/admin event inspect <world>" the 
admin should be teleported into the event world in spectator mode (like "/admin event review <world>" just with building world instead of submitted
ones).

Event settings:
Additionally to the current settings the builder has in event worlds there should be some new ones. First the player should be able to set the pvp
status of the paticipants. This should set the participants into the set pvp status overriding the server default and also interupting any pending
change. Also the players should not be able to change their pvp status inside of event worlds. When players leave the event world they should get 
the status back they had before joining the world. If they had a change pending this change won't be startet again automatically and the status will
be set to whatever it was before the pending got initiated. The builder should also be able to set a spawn point inside the event world. This can be
done by standing at the spawn location and then hitting a button in the menu or typing a command. Every player that joins the event should spawn at
at this set location and it should also serve as respawn point (as long as there is no other point determined by things like beds). Also the builder
should be able to change their own gamemode inside of event worlds through the menu and a command.

Event organizer:
When the event is active the builder should still be able to change every setting and these settings should also be applied to every player 
instantly, of them having to rejoin the event for the changes to take effect.

Event tools:
The builders should be able to build with special operator blocks. Since they aren't admin on the server they normally don't have acces to these 
items. Therefore in the menu there should be a new submenu where there is a list of these items and when the player clicks one of them he should
receive them. If his inventory is full he should receive an error message advising him to clear an inventory slot. The player should also be able to 
receive the items via "/event item <item>". This functionallity should obviously only be accessible inside of event world during the building phase.
The items players should be able to receive through this are: Barrier, Structure Void, Debug Stick, Light (every level), Painting (Earth, Fire,
Water, Wind).

Player World:
When players are in event worlds the diamond amount in the tab bar should be replaced with the event name. This name should also be colored in
regards to the current state of the event. BUILDING -> yellow, ACTIVE -> green, REVIEW -> gray. If the name is longer than 15 symbols, only the first
12 should be shown followed by "...".

Image Upload:
Players should be able to create maps of images. This should be possible through the player being able to select a file on their local file system 
through the client mod and then send this image to the the server through diawars:image payload. Before the image is send the client should resize 
the image to 128x128 pixels and then send it to the server. For this the image should be split in parts and send part by part so the every payload
end up being not to large. In the menu there should be a new submenu where the uploaded images are listet and the player can receive a map with the
image by clicking on the right one. Every player should only see their own images and also only be able the get the maps with their own images 
(Exchanging the items afterwards it of course fine). Instead of having to use the gui the player should also be able to get their images by using
"/image <file>". Every player should only be able to upload 20 full images to the server. When exceeding this limit the player gets and error telling
him to ask an admin to increase his limit when trying to upload any additional images. Admins can increase or decrease the limits of idividual 
players by using "/admin image limit inc|dec <player>". The command changes the limit by 10 images. If the new new limit is lower than the current
amount of uploaded images the images are kept and new uploads are just treated as if the limit is full. The limit obviously can't go under 0. Admins
should also be able to get a list of every player with their current amount of uploaded images and their limit by using "/admin image list". This
list should exclude every player whose image count is zero (exept if their limit is also 0). Admins should also be able to inspect individual images
of players. For this they should type "/admin image list <player>" to get a list of the images the player currently has stored. Then the admin can
inspect individual images by typing "/admin image inspect <player> <file>". Also admins can remove images by using "/admin image remove <player>
<file>" or by using "/admin image remove <player> all". Therefore files can't be named "all" and also not named the same as files already uploaded
by the player. Identical file names between different players should be allowed because internally the files should be saved in different folders.
[Additional context: For this change you also have to change the fabric and forge client side mod which can be found in the parent dir]
